{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0001","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000034-S02","priority":"medium","normative_level":"should","statement":"For example, if an element specifies that its contents should be numeric, a validation error will result from entering text.","topic_tags":["error_semantics"],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L115-L115"}}
{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0002","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000053-S01","priority":"low","normative_level":"may","statement":"InfoPath solves a problem in the area of data gathering that could not be solved before the advent of XML: by providing forms that can grow by adding optional groups of fields and by using the hierarchical data model of XML, InfoPath adds the flexibility of word processor documents to the rigorous validation features of a forms application.","topic_tags":[],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L150"}}
{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0003","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000067-S01","priority":"high","normative_level":"must","statement":"Because XML is extensible, you must do some up-front work to make support of XML in the Microsoft Office System work in your organization.","topic_tags":[],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L175-L175"}}
{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0004","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000067-S02","priority":"high","normative_level":"must","statement":"For example, you must define the XML elements that data in documents will map to, and you must define the logic that uses that data.","topic_tags":[],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L175-L175"}}
{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0005","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000069-S01","priority":"high","normative_level":"must","statement":"In order to map XML elements to Word 2003 documents, a valid XML Schema must be designed.","topic_tags":[],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L179-L179"}}
{"item_id":"CONF-office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-0006","document_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9","source_sentence_id":"office2003-xml-desktop-aa159914-v-office-11-901de7e9-SEG-000069-S02","priority":"high","normative_level":"must","statement":"Careful consideration must be put into the design of the schema in order to support all variations of the document template.","topic_tags":[],"verification_hint":"doc_to_probe_mapping_review","status":"candidate","source":{"source_id":"OFFICE2003-XML-DESKTOP","source_url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/office/developer/office-2003/aa159914(v=office.11)","local_path":"C:\\Work\\DnaCalc\\Foundation\\reference\\downloads\\learn.microsoft.com\\en-us\\previous-versions\\office\\developer\\office-2003\\aa159914(v=office.11).md","anchor":"L179-L179"}}
